		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_WONDER_FORUM_HELP">
			<Text>Provides +3 [ICON_RES_ROMANSTATUE] Roman statues. Grants 1 free Social Policy. Gives a free Market in this city and an additional Trade Route.</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_WONDER_FORUM_QUOTE">
			<Text>[NEWLINE]"I found Rome a city of bricks, and left it a city of marble."[NEWLINE] - Augustus Caesar[NEWLINE]</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_WONDER_FORUM_PEDIA">
			<Text>The Roman Forum is a rectangular forum (plaza) surrounded by the ruins of several important ancient government buildings at the center of the city of Rome. It was for centuries the center of Roman public life: the site of triumphal processions and elections; the venue for public speeches, criminal trials, and gladiatorial matches; and the nucleus of commercial affairs. Located in the small valley between the Palatine and Capitoline Hills, the Forum today is a sprawling ruin of architectural fragments and intermittent archeological excavations attracting numerous sightseers.</Text>
		</Row>
